total` e `_wait_ms_max` em `metrics`. Uma medição do runtime num repositório real, com os limiares fixados antes dos números, é `POSE_RUNTIME_MEASURE=<arquivo> go test ./internal/cli -run TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository`; o relatório fica em `.pose/reports/`.\\n\\n**Rodadas de review.** As rodadas de um escopo são os bundles selados em que uma review delegada concluída terminou, na ordem em que esses runs terminaram; `pose review verify`, `pose delegate ls` e `pose insights` mostram a rodada. A partir da rodada 2, o brief gerado (template `review-brief/2`; runs com `review-brief/1` continuam verificando) traz uma seção `Previous round` construída do ledger: cada finding aberto com o identificador que mantém entre rodadas (`R<rodada>-<id>`), sua severidade, disposição e local, o run anterior e o digest do seu draft. O draft do revisor é o bloco de código cercado cuja info string é `pose-draft`: JSON com `schema` `pose.review.draft/v1`, `decision` e `findings` (`id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line`, `summary`), e a partir da rodada 2 `prior_findings` (`id`, `status` fixed|partial|not-fixed|superseded, `evidence`) e `sweep`. Um finding reportado `partial` ou `not-fixed` mantém seu identificador no brief seguinte. Um draft da rodada 2 em diante que deixa um finding aberto sem conta, marca um como `fixed` sem evidência ou não declara a varredura é registrado com `draft_problems`, o `wait` o reporta como `invalid`, e ele nunca é aceito como aprovação. Com `routing.rounds` `continue-thread` (o padrão), uma rodada retoma a sessão com que a rodada anterior terminou, pelo comando de resume do agente; ela abre uma sessão nova, registrando o motivo, quando o agente ou seu vendor muda, a cadeia de drafts está quebrada, essa sessão não pode ser retomada, ou a rodada atinge `routing.round_threshold` (5 por padrão), onde o `verify` também avisa que as rodadas não estão convergindo. `cold-session` abre uma sessão nova a cada rodada. Cada run registra sua `round` e sua `thread`; `pose insights` reporta, por escopo, findings por rodada, rodadas até a aprovação, e como os findings anteriores foram contabilizados em rodadas continuadas e frias. Uma rodada anterior cujo registro não está íntegro faz o brief recusar.","numLines":1,"startLine":944,"totalLines":1071}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BNg5tEA9YGFEP8c5CqQKqY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtzgM4WY8UJro58zizaZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CkHZHRsivts3bto4nXL91o","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4170863541/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go","offset":225,"limit":130},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":39067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1815},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e379f4b8-495a-4115-adb2-42509e41d705","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:16:36.645Z","request_id":"req_011CgtzgLvKXAj3gzznSEkrr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CkHZHRsivts3bto4nXL91o":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4170863541/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go","offset":225,"limit":130}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CkHZHRsivts3bto4nXL91o","type":"tool_result","content":"225\t\ttime.Sleep(300 * time.Millisecond)\n226\t\tif ran.Load() != 1 {\n227\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runtime ran %d commands: the refused one ran later\", ran.Load())\n228\t\t}\n229\t}\n230\t\n231\t// R6: a short query is not queued behind a heavy check, and a full lane refuses before it waits.\n232\tfunc TestAShortQueryIsNotQueuedBehindAHeavyCheckAndAFullLaneRefuses(t *testing.T) {\n233\t\tf := newRuntimeFixture(t)\n234\t\tf.start(t, \"--heavy-slots\", \"1\", \"--heavy-queue\", \"0\")\n235\t\toriginal := runtimeHostedRun.Load()\n236\t\tslow := hostedRunFunc(func(args []string, out, errb io.Writer) int {\n237\t\t\tif args[0] == \"closeout-check\" {\n238\t\t\t\ttime.Sleep(900 * time.Millisecond)\n239\t\t\t}\n240\t\t\treturn (*original)(args, out, errb)\n241\t\t})\n242\t\truntimeHostedRun.Store(&slow)\n243\t\tdefer func() {\n244\t\t\ttime.Sleep(1200 * time.Millisecond)\n245\t\t\truntimeHostedRun.Store(original)\n246\t\t}()\n247\t\theavy := make(chan map[string]any, 1)\n248\t\tgo func() { doc, _, _ := f.run(\"closeout-check\"); heavy <- doc }()\n249\t\ttime.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)\n250\t\tstarted := time.Now()\n251\t\tshort, _, _ := f.run(\"surface-check\", \"--help\")\n252\t\tif short[\"via\"] != \"runtime\" || time.Since(started) > 600*time.Millisecond {\n253\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a short query waited for the heavy check: %v after %v\", short[\"via\"], time.Since(started))\n254\t\t}\n255\t\tfull, _, _ := f.run(\"closeout-check\")\n256\t\tif full[\"via\"] != \"standalone\" || !strings.Contains(full[\"fallback_reason\"].(string), \"lane of the runtime is full\") {\n257\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a full heavy lane: %v\", full)\n258\t\t}\n259\t\tif d := <-heavy; d[\"via\"] != \"runtime\" {\n260\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the first heavy check: %v\", d)\n261\t\t}\n262\t\tid, err := worktreeruntime.ResolveIdentity(f.root, version.Version, runtimeBuild())\n263\t\tif err != nil {\n264\t\t\tt.Skip(err)\n265\t\t}\n266\t\t// The command's own status says it too, in JSON and in the human output.\n267\t\tvar jsonOut, humanOut bytes.Buffer\n268\t\tcmdRuntime(f.root, []string{\"status\", \"--json\"}, &jsonOut, io.Discard)\n269\t\tvar doc struct {\n270\t\t\tMetrics map[string]int64 `json:\"metrics\"`\n271\t\t}\n272\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(jsonOut.Bytes(), &doc); err != nil || doc.Metrics[\"heavy_refused\"] != 1 || doc.Metrics[\"short_admitted\"] != 1 {\n273\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pose runtime status --json does not carry the lane metrics: %s\", jsonOut.String())\n274\t\t}\n275\t\tcmdRuntime(f.root, []string{\"status\"}, &humanOut, io.Discard)\n276\t\tif !strings.Contains(humanOut.String(), \"runtime.metrics.heavy_refused=1\") {\n277\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pose runtime status does not print the lane metrics: %s\", humanOut.String())\n278\t\t}\n279\t\tstatus, err := worktreeruntime.Client{Identity: id, Dir: worktreeruntime.DefaultDir()}.Status(context.Background())\n280\t\tif err != nil || status.Metrics[\"heavy_refused\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"heavy_admitted\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"short_admitted\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"heavy_slots\"] != 1 {\n281\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the metrics do not say what happened: %+v %v\", status.Metrics, err)\n282\t\t}\n283\t}\n284\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"ad2089e4-3cbb-4fc9-9426-d5eac7e6b618","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:16:36.652Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4170863541/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go","content":"\ttime.Sleep(300 * time.Millisecond)\n\tif ran.Load() != 1 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runtime ran %d commands: the refused one ran later\", ran.Load())\n\t}\n}\n\n// R6: a short query is not queued behind a heavy check, and a full lane refuses before it waits.\nfunc TestAShortQueryIsNotQueuedBehindAHeavyCheckAndAFullLaneRefuses(t *testing.T) {\n\tf := newRuntimeFixture(t)\n\tf.start(t, \"--heavy-slots\", \"1\", \"--heavy-queue\", \"0\")\n\toriginal := runtimeHostedRun.Load()\n\tslow := hostedRunFunc(func(args []string, out, errb io.Writer) int {\n\t\tif args[0] == \"closeout-check\" {\n\t\t\ttime.Sleep(900 * time.Millisecond)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn (*original)(args, out, errb)\n\t})\n\truntimeHostedRun.Store(&slow)\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\ttime.Sleep(1200 * time.Millisecond)\n\t\truntimeHostedRun.Store(original)\n\t}()\n\theavy := make(chan map[string]any, 1)\n\tgo func() { doc, _, _ := f.run(\"closeout-check\"); heavy <- doc }()\n\ttime.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)\n\tstarted := time.Now()\n\tshort, _, _ := f.run(\"surface-check\", \"--help\")\n\tif short[\"via\"] != \"runtime\" || time.Since(started) > 600*time.Millisecond {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a short query waited for the heavy check: %v after %v\", short[\"via\"], time.Since(started))\n\t}\n\tfull, _, _ := f.run(\"closeout-check\")\n\tif full[\"via\"] != \"standalone\" || !strings.Contains(full[\"fallback_reason\"].(string), \"lane of the runtime is full\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a full heavy lane: %v\", full)\n\t}\n\tif d := <-heavy; d[\"via\"] != \"runtime\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the first heavy check: %v\", d)\n\t}\n\tid, err := worktreeruntime.ResolveIdentity(f.root, version.Version, runtimeBuild())\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(err)\n\t}\n\t// The command's own status says it too, in JSON and in the human output.\n\tvar jsonOut, humanOut bytes.Buffer\n\tcmdRuntime(f.root, []string{\"status\", \"--json\"}, &jsonOut, io.Discard)\n\tvar doc struct {\n\t\tMetrics map[string]int64 `json:\"metrics\"`\n\t}\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(jsonOut.Bytes(), &doc); err != nil || doc.Metrics[\"heavy_refused\"] != 1 || doc.Metrics[\"short_admitted\"] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pose runtime status --json does not carry the lane metrics: %s\", jsonOut.String())\n\t}\n\tcmdRuntime(f.root, []string{\"status\"}, &humanOut, io.Discard)\n\tif !strings.Contains(humanOut.String(), \"runtime.metrics.heavy_refused=1\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pose runtime status does not print the lane metrics: %s\", humanOut.String())\n\t}\n\tstatus, err := worktreeruntime.Client{Identity: id, Dir: worktreeruntime.DefaultDir()}.Status(context.Background())\n\tif err != nil || status.Metrics[\"heavy_refused\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"heavy_admitted\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"short_admitted\"] != 1 || status.Metrics[\"heavy_slots\"] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the metrics do not say what happened: %+v %v\", status.Metrics, err)\n\t}\n}\n","numLines":60,"startLine":225,"totalLines":284}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CkHZHRsivts3bto4nXL91o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
