{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgtzz22mgzmqgqSUq3Yuf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**decision: approved**\n\nAll three round-1 blockers are fixed. I found no high or medium defects in this round. What's left is low-severity, and each item is a follow-up with an owner and a review date.\n\n## Previous findings\n- **R1-F1: fixed.** `runtime_cmd.go:249-251` adds `metrics` to `status --json`, and `:266-273` prints it as `runtime.metrics.*`. `runtime_host_test.go:266-278` checks both outputs. The run-2 JSON report has a filled `runtime_metrics` (line 172).\n- **R1-F2: fixed.** POSE.md:949 and locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 now say \"in the admission lanes described below\". A search of all four POSE.md copies no longer finds \"one hosted command at a time\".\n- **R1-F3: fixed.** Report `.md:53` gives the effective figures: heavy lane 7 admitted, short lane 20 admitted, 0 refused, 0 ms wait. These match the counts the harness produces (1+5+1 heavy, 10+10 short).\n- **R1-F4: partial.** The comment at `runtime_host.go:78` was updated, but `runtime_host.go:97` still says \"One hosted command at a time\". The concurrency proof is still only `surface-check --help` (`runtime_host_test.go:251`). It is recorded as a follow-up in spec line 131.\n- **R1-F5: not-fixed.** `runtime_host.go:128,139,146` still reports `memo_hits` as the change in a counter shared by the whole process. It is accepted as a follow-up in spec line 131.\n- **R1-F6: fixed.** `runtime_measure_test.go:186-201` compares the short query with standalone, both idle and under load.\n- **R1-F7: fixed.** `runtime_measure_test.go:217-238` reads VmHWM after the concurrent phase.\n\n## New findings (all low, follow-up)\n- **N1** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:128`: the usage text still lists only `--idle`, `--drain` and `--json`. It leaves out the five new admission flags.\n- **N2** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_lanes.go:23`: when GOMAXPROCS < 2, the default short-lane slots quietly drop to 1. R6 and POSE.md:949 say the default is 2.\n- **N3** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:196`: the heavy `review-check` that runs alongside the short queries throws away its `via` and its output. The T5 verdict text (line 267) still says every hosted run matched standalone.\n- **N4** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:175`: `restart` starts `serve` again with default admission settings, so any non-default settings from the earlier `start` are lost. Separately, `status`, `stop` and `attach` accept the admission flags and silently ignore them. Neither behaviour is documented.\n- **N5** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:78-89`: nothing tests the error path for bad values (`--heavy-slots 0`, a value that isn't a number, a missing value).\n\n## Criteria\n- **Thresholds T1–T6:** identical in the spec (R8), the test constants (`runtime_measure_test.go:32-37`) and both report runs. All six passed.\n- **Classification:** `shortCommands` contains only `surface-check`, which matches D1 and the timings stated in the spec.\n- **Known gaps:** the simultaneous-arrival gap is stated honestly. The check at `runtime_lanes.go:58` (queue full *and* every slot busy) is the cause, and Go's channel handoff keeps the window small.\n- **Refusal leads to standalone:** a lane-full refusal comes back as `OutcomeRefused`, and `runtime_host.go:209-210` then runs the command standalone.\n- **Plan tools:** I ran `artifact-check --strict` (only orphan warnings for files outside this change) and `surface-check --strict` (0 findings). This profile refused `assess design`, `git diff` and the other shell commands. I did not run `pose validate` myself; for it I rely on the sealed evidence.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 128, \"summary\": \"The usage string of pose runtime omits --heavy-slots, --short-slots, --heavy-queue, --short-queue and --memo-mib.\", \"action\": \"Add the admission flags to the runtime usage string in both locales.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_lanes.go\", \"line\": 23, \"summary\": \"Default short slots silently become 1 when GOMAXPROCS < 2; R6 and POSE.md:949 state a default of 2 without that exception.\", \"action\": \"Document the single-CPU default in R6 and the four POSE.md copies, or drop the special case.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 196, \"summary\": \"The concurrent heavy review-check discards its via and output, so the T5 verdict (line 267) does not cover the heavy run under concurrency, and the harness never confirms that the load really ran in the runtime.\", \"action\": \"Assert via == runtime and output == coldOut for the concurrent heavy run.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 175, \"summary\": \"restart starts serve again with default admission unless the flags are repeated, dropping a previous non-default configuration; status/stop/attach accept the admission flags and silently ignore them. Neither behaviour is documented.\", \"action\": \"Document that restart takes the admission flags (and defaults without them), or refuse the admission flags on subcommands that ignore them.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 78, \"summary\": \"No test covers the admission-flag error path (out-of-range, non-numeric or missing values).\", \"action\": \"Add a table test of parseRuntimeFlags for invalid admission values.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:249-251 (JSON metrics) and :266-273 (human runtime.metrics.*); tested at pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go:266-278; .pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.json:172 has runtime_metrics filled\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"POSE.md:949 and locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 now say 'in the admission lanes described below'; a search for 'one hosted command at a time' over all four POSE.md copies finds no match\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:53 states the effective metrics (heavy 7 admitted / short 20 admitted, 0 refused, 0 ms max wait), consistent with the harness counts\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"evidence\": \"The comment at pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:78 was updated, but runtime_host.go:97 still reads 'One hosted command at a time'; the concurrency proof is still surface-check --help (runtime_host_test.go:251); recorded as a follow-up in spec line 131\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F5\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:128,139,146 still report the change in the process-wide ResidentGitMemoStats counter; accepted as a low follow-up in spec line 131 (owner @pose-maintainers, review 2027-02-08)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F6\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:186-201 compares the surface-check output idle and under load with shortStandalone\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F7\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:217-238 reads VmHWM after the concurrent phase (lines 194-205)\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read the spec (R6, R8, D1, known gaps, final report); runtime_lanes.go in full; runtime_host.go in full; the diff of runtime_cmd.go and worktreeruntime/runtime.go (flags, serveArgs, start/restart spawn, status report, Options.Metrics); runtime_host_test.go R6 test; runtime_measure_test.go in full (thresholds against spec and report, scenarios, T3/T4/T5 ordering); both report runs (.md and .json verdicts and metrics); POSE.md and pt-BR paragraphs and the scaffold copies for stale wording; usage and help strings; ran pose artifact-check --strict and pose surface-check --strict.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Verified: thresholds T1-T6 identical in spec R8, runtime_measure_test.go:32-37 and both report runs; classification surface-check=short matches the measured timings. Unresolved and stated: one environment and repository, the race at the last free slot, no per-command CPU/memory limit, short defaults tuned to the measured machine. Accepted risks are low follow-ups (R1-F4, R1-F5, N1-N5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"pose.runtime.status/1 only gains an optional 'metrics' field (omitempty in Reply); runtimeSpawn's signature is internal; the new flags are additive with defaults; the run envelope is unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f\", \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses the cause (one global semaphore in slice 2 made a 10 ms surface-check wait for a 25 s review-check) with per-lane slot channels (runtime_lanes.go:47-52) chosen by a declared, measured list (shortCommands); queue bound and refusal before waiting (enter, runtime_host.go:107-109) meet the falsifier.\", \"mappings\": [{\"delta\": \"design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The structural change (new runtime_lanes.go, handler gated by lanes, Options.Metrics) is the selected option of D1 for R6 and R8.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The changed files match the spec's artifact list; there are no cgroup limits or durable queue (non-goals respected); the governance index churn is generated.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Flag values are bounded to 0/1..1048576; metrics are counters only, with no paths or secrets; env-digest and hosted-command refusal precede lane entry (runtime_host.go:90-95), so admission adds no authority.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The smallest sufficient alternative (D1 minimal: one command at a time) fails the stated 10 ms vs 25 s cause. Two lanes from a static map plus channels and atomics are about 110 lines, with no scheduler. Invalidating condition: a hosted command that is not safe to run concurrently in-process, or a short command that becomes slow.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it; only repository-wide orphan warnings for files outside this change, no errors.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"The review profile refused the command; I relied on sealed structure:design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the profile did not allow it and the change is confined to the runtime package.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; covered by sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; not needed to judge this scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the files to review were read directly.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Also ran pose surface-check --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --strict: 1 target, 204 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on the sealed validation evidence (build, unit, integration, e2e all pass); not re-run under this profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on the sealed pose-mcp module evidence; not re-run under this profile.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":66191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"53013590-4d27-4ccf-974d-565386060062","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:21:18.935Z","request_id":"req_011Cgtzz1tqaYPwuErtTsmwq"}
{"duration_api_ms":128447,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":0.9432658,"usage":{"input_tokens":38,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60955,"cache_read_input_tokens":846269,"output_tokens":14311,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4329},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5654,"cache_read_input_tokens":66191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":38,"outputTokens":14311,"cacheReadInputTokens":846269,"cacheCreationInputTokens":60955,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9432658,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4329,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":60955,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D7KDYFiYPGc9rRcd78vhcZ","tool_input":{"command":"cd /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4170863541/worktree && git diff 4b5ec690f15b..6aec91f6 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd_test.go POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md; diff POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md >/dev/null && echo SAME_EN; diff locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md >/dev/null && echo SAME_PT","description":"Show test and doc diffs, compare scaffold copies"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_0194dGFibZbhtR7prZ9Ajztp","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess design --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --json | head -c 4000","timeout":300000,"description":"Run the plan's design assessment"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_013crbe1YaZbQfa4Tyf8jkCy","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess design --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --json","timeout":300000,"description":"Run the plan's design assessment"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**decision: approved**\n\nAll three round-1 blockers are fixed. I found no high or medium defects in this round. What's left is low-severity, and each item is a follow-up with an owner and a review date.\n\n## Previous findings\n- **R1-F1: fixed.** `runtime_cmd.go:249-251` adds `metrics` to `status --json`, and `:266-273` prints it as `runtime.metrics.*`. `runtime_host_test.go:266-278` checks both outputs. The run-2 JSON report has a filled `runtime_metrics` (line 172).\n- **R1-F2: fixed.** POSE.md:949 and locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 now say \"in the admission lanes described below\". A search of all four POSE.md copies no longer finds \"one hosted command at a time\".\n- **R1-F3: fixed.** Report `.md:53` gives the effective figures: heavy lane 7 admitted, short lane 20 admitted, 0 refused, 0 ms wait. These match the counts the harness produces (1+5+1 heavy, 10+10 short).\n- **R1-F4: partial.** The comment at `runtime_host.go:78` was updated, but `runtime_host.go:97` still says \"One hosted command at a time\". The concurrency proof is still only `surface-check --help` (`runtime_host_test.go:251`). It is recorded as a follow-up in spec line 131.\n- **R1-F5: not-fixed.** `runtime_host.go:128,139,146` still reports `memo_hits` as the change in a counter shared by the whole process. It is accepted as a follow-up in spec line 131.\n- **R1-F6: fixed.** `runtime_measure_test.go:186-201` compares the short query with standalone, both idle and under load.\n- **R1-F7: fixed.** `runtime_measure_test.go:217-238` reads VmHWM after the concurrent phase.\n\n## New findings (all low, follow-up)\n- **N1** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:128`: the usage text still lists only `--idle`, `--drain` and `--json`. It leaves out the five new admission flags.\n- **N2** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_lanes.go:23`: when GOMAXPROCS < 2, the default short-lane slots quietly drop to 1. R6 and POSE.md:949 say the default is 2.\n- **N3** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:196`: the heavy `review-check` that runs alongside the short queries throws away its `via` and its output. The T5 verdict text (line 267) still says every hosted run matched standalone.\n- **N4** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:175`: `restart` starts `serve` again with default admission settings, so any non-default settings from the earlier `start` are lost. Separately, `status`, `stop` and `attach` accept the admission flags and silently ignore them. Neither behaviour is documented.\n- **N5** `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:78-89`: nothing tests the error path for bad values (`--heavy-slots 0`, a value that isn't a number, a missing value).\n\n## Criteria\n- **Thresholds T1–T6:** identical in the spec (R8), the test constants (`runtime_measure_test.go:32-37`) and both report runs. All six passed.\n- **Classification:** `shortCommands` contains only `surface-check`, which matches D1 and the timings stated in the spec.\n- **Known gaps:** the simultaneous-arrival gap is stated honestly. The check at `runtime_lanes.go:58` (queue full *and* every slot busy) is the cause, and Go's channel handoff keeps the window small.\n- **Refusal leads to standalone:** a lane-full refusal comes back as `OutcomeRefused`, and `runtime_host.go:209-210` then runs the command standalone.\n- **Plan tools:** I ran `artifact-check --strict` (only orphan warnings for files outside this change) and `surface-check --strict` (0 findings). This profile refused `assess design`, `git diff` and the other shell commands. I did not run `pose validate` myself; for it I rely on the sealed evidence.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 128, \"summary\": \"The usage string of pose runtime omits --heavy-slots, --short-slots, --heavy-queue, --short-queue and --memo-mib.\", \"action\": \"Add the admission flags to the runtime usage string in both locales.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_lanes.go\", \"line\": 23, \"summary\": \"Default short slots silently become 1 when GOMAXPROCS < 2; R6 and POSE.md:949 state a default of 2 without that exception.\", \"action\": \"Document the single-CPU default in R6 and the four POSE.md copies, or drop the special case.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 196, \"summary\": \"The concurrent heavy review-check discards its via and output, so the T5 verdict (line 267) does not cover the heavy run under concurrency, and the harness never confirms that the load really ran in the runtime.\", \"action\": \"Assert via == runtime and output == coldOut for the concurrent heavy run.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 175, \"summary\": \"restart starts serve again with default admission unless the flags are repeated, dropping a previous non-default configuration; status/stop/attach accept the admission flags and silently ignore them. Neither behaviour is documented.\", \"action\": \"Document that restart takes the admission flags (and defaults without them), or refuse the admission flags on subcommands that ignore them.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go\", \"line\": 78, \"summary\": \"No test covers the admission-flag error path (out-of-range, non-numeric or missing values).\", \"action\": \"Add a table test of parseRuntimeFlags for invalid admission values.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_cmd.go:249-251 (JSON metrics) and :266-273 (human runtime.metrics.*); tested at pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host_test.go:266-278; .pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.json:172 has runtime_metrics filled\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"POSE.md:949 and locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 now say 'in the admission lanes described below'; a search for 'one hosted command at a time' over all four POSE.md copies finds no match\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:53 states the effective metrics (heavy 7 admitted / short 20 admitted, 0 refused, 0 ms max wait), consistent with the harness counts\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"evidence\": \"The comment at pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:78 was updated, but runtime_host.go:97 still reads 'One hosted command at a time'; the concurrency proof is still surface-check --help (runtime_host_test.go:251); recorded as a follow-up in spec line 131\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F5\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:128,139,146 still report the change in the process-wide ResidentGitMemoStats counter; accepted as a low follow-up in spec line 131 (owner @pose-maintainers, review 2027-02-08)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F6\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:186-201 compares the surface-check output idle and under load with shortStandalone\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F7\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:217-238 reads VmHWM after the concurrent phase (lines 194-205)\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read the spec (R6, R8, D1, known gaps, final report); runtime_lanes.go in full; runtime_host.go in full; the diff of runtime_cmd.go and worktreeruntime/runtime.go (flags, serveArgs, start/restart spawn, status report, Options.Metrics); runtime_host_test.go R6 test; runtime_measure_test.go in full (thresholds against spec and report, scenarios, T3/T4/T5 ordering); both report runs (.md and .json verdicts and metrics); POSE.md and pt-BR paragraphs and the scaffold copies for stale wording; usage and help strings; ran pose artifact-check --strict and pose surface-check --strict.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Verified: thresholds T1-T6 identical in spec R8, runtime_measure_test.go:32-37 and both report runs; classification surface-check=short matches the measured timings. Unresolved and stated: one environment and repository, the race at the last free slot, no per-command CPU/memory limit, short defaults tuned to the measured machine. Accepted risks are low follow-ups (R1-F4, R1-F5, N1-N5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"pose.runtime.status/1 only gains an optional 'metrics' field (omitempty in Reply); runtimeSpawn's signature is internal; the new flags are additive with defaults; the run envelope is unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f\", \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses the cause (one global semaphore in slice 2 made a 10 ms surface-check wait for a 25 s review-check) with per-lane slot channels (runtime_lanes.go:47-52) chosen by a declared, measured list (shortCommands); queue bound and refusal before waiting (enter, runtime_host.go:107-109) meet the falsifier.\", \"mappings\": [{\"delta\": \"design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The structural change (new runtime_lanes.go, handler gated by lanes, Options.Metrics) is the selected option of D1 for R6 and R8.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The changed files match the spec's artifact list; there are no cgroup limits or durable queue (non-goals respected); the governance index churn is generated.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Flag values are bounded to 0/1..1048576; metrics are counters only, with no paths or secrets; env-digest and hosted-command refusal precede lane entry (runtime_host.go:90-95), so admission adds no authority.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The smallest sufficient alternative (D1 minimal: one command at a time) fails the stated 10 ms vs 25 s cause. Two lanes from a static map plus channels and atomics are about 110 lines, with no scheduler. Invalidating condition: a hosted command that is not safe to run concurrently in-process, or a short command that becomes slow.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it; only repository-wide orphan warnings for files outside this change, no errors.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"The review profile refused the command; I relied on sealed structure:design-c96df3d8a0d0c17f.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the profile did not allow it and the change is confined to the runtime package.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; covered by sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; not needed to judge this scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the files to review were read directly.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Also ran pose surface-check --spec pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement --strict: 1 target, 204 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on the sealed validation evidence (build, unit, integration, e2e all pass); not re-run under this profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on the sealed pose-mcp module evidence; not re-run under this profile.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1440,"type":"result","duration_ms":314463,"uuid":"bb64b483-89e4-4228-824d-8aee3066e4ad","ttft_stream_ms":676,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":676,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":38,"outputTokens":14311,"cacheReadInputTokens":846269,"cacheCreationInputTokens":60955,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9432658,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4329,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":60955,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04